          <change when="2023-10-19T05:17:24-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/Fran%C3%A7ois%20Gerardin">Submit - I have integrated all corrections of the BL (2.2.48, 5.25, and 8.90). &#xD;
Note that based on my own inspection of the digital photograph l. 6-7 I have given preference to Vitelli's readings over Schubart's (both recorded at BL 2.2.48) but retained the original reading ἐπὶ ο[ὖν] (emended to ἐπὶ οὖ[ν]) instead of Vitelli's restoration as ἐπὶ [δέ]. The omicron is clear and traces of the upsilon still visible. I have tried to record all these readings as carefully as possible in the apparatus.&#xD;
I have also deleted the date (180-192 CE) from the metadata since the correct date is now certainly 180-181 CE, following Bingen BL 5 25, but haven't been able to put the correct one. </change>
